From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] voicecall: answer headset commands on the modem that has the call

voicecall registers its headset commands on every emulator atom of its
modem, and with one emulator for both SIMs the command may arrive at the
voicecall of the modem without the call: ATA for a call ringing on the
second SIM then answers ERROR, and AT+CHUP hangs up nothing.

Pick the voicecall for each command among all modems the emulator
serves:

  ATA                   the modem with an incoming call
  AT+CHUP, AT+CHLD,     the modem with a call or a dial in progress
  ATD, AT+BLDN
  AT+VTS                the modem with a call that can send DTMF

and fall back to the voicecall that owns the handler when no modem
matches. AT+CLCC lists the calls of every modem.
__ofono_emulator_foreach_modem() walks the modems an emulator serves,
in the order they were added.

ATD with no call anywhere dials on the first modem the emulator serves,
which is the first modem hfp_ag_bluez5 saw become ready. Sailfish dials
on the modem whose voicecall registered the "D" handler last. Neither
asks the default voice modem setting, which lives outside the core.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending

